# The site's copy of the data is generated, not authored.
#
# data/jobs.json and site/data/jobs.json held byte-identical content and both
# were committed on every scrape - ninety-six commits a day, three megabytes
# apiece. Between them they accounted for 105 MB of the repository's history
# for one board of jobs. The pipeline still writes site/data locally so the
# site can be served straight from a checkout, but the published copy is now
# built in the workflow at deploy time instead of being carried in git.
site/data/

